<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίγῠος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχος,</span> either
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυῖον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with a limb at each end, double-pointed,</i> or
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γύης</span>) <i>bending both ways,
				elastic,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.147
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.527
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δούρασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.135
				</span></i>
			; prob. (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυῖον</span>)
				<i>stout rivals,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				504
			</span></i>(lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
